---
import StarlightPage from '@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro';
---
<StarlightPage frontmatter={{ title: 'Lens reviewer dispatch (stub)' }}>
  <h1>Lens reviewer dispatch flow</h1>
  <div class="callout-warn">
    <strong>Stubbed for follow-up.</strong> This page will render the
    <code>lens-agents</code> dispatch flow (architect / adversarial / behavior /
    delivery lenses → per-lens prompt overlay → reviewer agent → consolidated
    review).
  </div>
  <p>
    Tracked in the <code>pr-a-lens-agents</code> worktree and the
    <code>thermo-nuclear-lens-evaluation</code> task. Once that work lands,
    a structured graph view will replace this stub.
  </p>
  <p>
    Until then, the source-of-truth for the lens dispatch contract is the
    <strong>Review stage</strong> section of the <code>isp</code> skill at
    <code>internal/scaffold/home/starter/skills/global/isp/instructions/staged-runtime.md</code>
    (three-lens contract: spawn one reviewer per lens), and the per-lens agent
    definitions under
    <code>internal/scaffold/home/starter/agents/global/&lt;lens&gt;-reviewer/AGENT.md</code>
    (<code>architecture-standards-reviewer</code>,
    <code>acceptance-invariants-reviewer</code>,
    <code>adversarial-reviewer</code>). Note: <code>commands/review.go</code> is
    the <code>da review</code> proposal-approval command — a different surface,
    not the lens dispatch contract.
  </p>
</StarlightPage>

<style>
  .callout-warn {
    border: 1px solid var(--sl-color-orange);
    border-left-width: 0.25rem;
    border-radius: 0.4rem;
    background: var(--sl-color-orange-low);
    color: var(--sl-color-orange-high);
    padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
    margin: 1rem 0;
  }
</style>
